UID:10021141-1779634800-1779642000@golocal.coop
SUMMARY:Victoria George & The High Lonesome with David Luning
DESCRIPTION:Sunday May 24 at 3 pm: Victoria George & The High Lonesome with David Luning at Occidental Center for the Arts. OCA is proud to present Victoria George and the High Lonesome\, with special guest David Luning in our amphitheater! Victoria George has carved out her own path as a singer-songwriter\, channeling a Northern California spirit into music that blends country roots and folk storytelling with hints of pop and rock. Born and raised in Marin County\, she stepped onto the stage in her teens and soon was fronting her own band and writing songs and sharing bills with Brandi Carlile\, Willie Nelson\, Loudon Wainwright\, The Doobie Brothers\, Gin Blossoms\, and Jackie Greene. Her fine band\, featuring Dave Sampson\, Mike Anderson and J.T. John\, will be celebrating the release of their album Wilderness.Tickets are $25 GA/Discount for OCA members at www.occidentalcenterforthearts.org. Free for kids 12 and under. Online sales end at 12:00 Noon day of show; tickets will be available at the gate. Bring your own seat cushion or low-backed chair. Wheelchair/ADA seating available\, contact info@occidentalcenterforthearts.org. Beer and wine\, refreshments for sale; Art Gallery open. 3850 Doris Murphy Ct. Occidental\, CA. 95465.
URL:https://golocal.coop/event/victoria-george-the-high-lonesome-with-david-luning/
LOCATION:Occidental Center for the Arts\, 3850 Doris Murphy Ct.\, Occidental
CATEGORIES:Music
